        <details class="sql-syntax-ref">
            <summary><i class="fa-solid fa-code"></i> Reference pattern — CREATE VIEW</summary>
            <div class="sql-syntax-body">
                <pre><code>CREATE VIEW useful_view AS
SELECT a.column_a, b.column_b, c.score_column
FROM first_table AS a
INNER JOIN link_table AS c
    ON a.primary_key = c.first_id
INNER JOIN second_table AS b
    ON c.second_id = b.primary_key
WHERE c.score_column >= 90;

SELECT *
FROM useful_view
ORDER BY score_column DESC;</code></pre>
                <p>A virtual view stores the query, not a second copy of the data. It can simplify long joins and hide unnecessary complexity from users.</p>
            </div>
        </details>

