    <section class="sql-sheet-section">
        <div class="sql-section-heading">
            <span class="sql-section-number">4</span>
            <div>
                <h2>Transactions and ACID</h2>
                <p>Use transaction control language to protect data integrity while changes are being made.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <details class="sql-syntax-ref">
            <summary><i class="fa-solid fa-code"></i> Reference pattern — BEGIN TRANSACTION, COMMIT, ROLLBACK</summary>
            <div class="sql-syntax-body">
                <pre><code>BEGIN TRANSACTION;

INSERT INTO parent_table (id, name_column)
VALUES (9001, 'New record');

INSERT INTO child_table (parent_id, item_id, score_column)
VALUES (9001, 501, 88);

COMMIT;

BEGIN TRANSACTION;
UPDATE child_table
SET score_column = 91
WHERE parent_id = 9001;
ROLLBACK;</code></pre>
                <p>Use <code>COMMIT</code> when all related changes should become permanent together. Use <code>ROLLBACK</code> when you need to undo the whole transaction.</p>
            </div>
        </details>

