            <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-unlock"></i> Model Answers — Course Enrolment</h2>

            <h3>Section 1</h3>
            <div class="sql-answer-item">
                <span class="sql-answer-num">1</span>
                <div class="sql-answer-body">
                    <strong>Recap answer</strong>
                    <code>ENROLLMENT</code> has the composite key <code>(StudentID, CourseID)</code>, representing which student is enrolled on which course.
                </div>
            </div>

            <h3>Section 2</h3>
            <div class="sql-answer-item">
                <span class="sql-answer-num">2</span>
                <div class="sql-answer-body">
                    <strong>Aggregate examples</strong>
                    <pre><code>SELECT d.DepartmentName, COUNT(*) AS EnrollmentCount
FROM ENROLLMENT AS e
INNER JOIN COURSE AS c
    ON e.CourseID = c.CourseID
INNER JOIN DEPARTMENT AS d
    ON c.DepartmentID = d.DepartmentID
GROUP BY d.DepartmentName
HAVING COUNT(*) >= 4;</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h3>Section 3</h3>
            <div class="sql-answer-item">
                <span class="sql-answer-num">3</span>
                <div class="sql-answer-body">
                    <strong>View pattern</strong>
                    <pre><code>CREATE VIEW HighScorers AS
SELECT s.FirstName, s.LastName, c.CourseName, d.DepartmentName, e.Score
FROM ENROLLMENT AS e
INNER JOIN STUDENT AS s
    ON e.StudentID = s.StudentID
INNER JOIN COURSE AS c
    ON e.CourseID = c.CourseID
INNER JOIN DEPARTMENT AS d
    ON c.DepartmentID = d.DepartmentID
WHERE e.Score >= 90;</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h3>Section 4</h3>
            <div class="sql-answer-item">
                <span class="sql-answer-num">4</span>
                <div class="sql-answer-body">
                    <strong>ACID summary</strong>
                    Atomicity keeps related changes together, consistency preserves valid states, isolation stops overlapping transactions from interfering, and durability keeps committed work safe after failure.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

